CVE-2026-44115 hides shell expansion in unquoted heredoc bodies so an allowlisted command evaluates more than it shows, rather than smuggling tokens in environment-variable names. Cyera's two scanner counts, about 65,000 on Shodan and 180,000 on Zoomeye, are separate figures, not 245,000 exposed servers, and its chain runs from a sandbox foothold through credential exposure and owner control to persistence through the write escape. All four flaws are fixed in openclaw release 2026.4.22, and the CVSS scores differ by scorer, with OpenClaw rating CVE-2026-44115 moderate.
